/* Solids sliced from real STL meshes by tools/stl-to-solid.mjs — not drawn by hand.

   A hand-authored polygon can approximate a vase (one profile, revolved) but never a
   3DBenchy or an articulated dragon: those are many DISCONNECTED islands per layer — cabin
   walls, a doorway, bulwarks; a vertebra, a rib, a horn — and no single outline stands in
   for that. These strings are the actual cut of the actual mesh at each printed layer.

   Format: layers separated by `|`, loops within a layer by `;`, coordinates as integers
   in thousandths of the bed width. Compact enough to sit in the entry bundle and trivial to
   regenerate — point the tool at any STL and paste the result here. */

